From: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:58:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 20/20] RISC OS: scale with the overlay (riscos-mesa
 20.3.5-17e)

System Options, General: "Scale with the overlay" (video.overlay). In
borderless full screen with a Resolution smaller than the screen, the
window is made with SDL_RISCOS_FB_RENDER_SIZE set to that Resolution and
SDL_RISCOS_FB_OVERLAY, so riscos-mesa scales the picture to the screen
through the Pi's VideoOverlay instead of the game showing it centred.
Decided when the window is made: changes take effect at the next start
(the game says so). If the render size isn't the one asked for (no EGL
surface), the picture is centred as before.

getScreenSize() gives the screen's size for the Resolution list and
the centred check, as the render size is smaller with the overlay.

video.centred and video.overlay are now in the schema's required list,
so they are saved: settings not listed there are dropped when
settings.json is written, so riscos7test forgot the centred playground
on the next start.
